rger_jarl_%28Forss%C3%A9n%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the 1260s Birger Jarl bore a ducal coronet and used the Latin title of Dux Sweorum (Latin for \"Duke of the Swedes\"); the design of his coronet combined those used by continental European and English dukes.[7]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABirger_jarl_(Forss%C3%A9n).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Bengt_Birgersson.JPG/500px-Bengt_Birgersson.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Bengt_Birgersson.JPG/1280px-Bengt_Birgersson.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Bengt_Birgersson.JPG/500px-Bengt_Birgersson.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bishop Bengt Birgersson (1254–1291) was the first Duke of Finland[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABengt_Birgersson.JPG"}],"sounds":{"grand duke":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-grand_duke.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/97/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-grand_duke.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-grand_duke.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/97/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-grand_duke.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-grand_duke.wav.ogg"}]}}}